# christmas eve hidden route culmination/early ending
# proceeds after all specific criteria under the hidden route (codenamed "dependence route") throughout the main story
# the school culture fest happens on october 25-26 (saturday afternoon to sunday afternoon). if the player meets all the criteria, the story automatically skips to christmas eve. the story will have deviating scenes before then, but this is the point of no return
# MC does not have any natural dialogue or narration in this scene, only player menus. tsubaki does all the on-screen talking
# tsubaki has her ruined sprites. technically, you as the player saved her from sam, but now MC acts as the narrative replacement due to seeding, nurturing, and exploiting tsubaki's dependency issues, even if you meant well.
# at this point, she has a planner with attached note cards, all with things that the player has had her depend on them for since the first dependency route scene back in chapter 0.5.
# the overall theme is that you can save people from tragedy, but sometimes said tragedy could just be the lesser of two evils. at this point, you have arguably become worse than Sam.
# tsubaki then comes clean about things she's realized: she hates matsuda. she hates asahina. she cannot STAND monika. she hates MC. she hates YOU.
# but at the same time, she feels liberated, knowing that she's more prone to following a more "free" path by depending on MC. the cruel irony is that she's still shackled in a prison, figuratively.
# the meta narrative that is implicit but answers a lot about this game's world (AGAIN, it's never explicitly stated) is that tsubaki knows what matsuda is trying to do.
# she knows that matsuda is trying to bend the story and the narrative to her control so that she can be the centerpiece she's always wanted to be. matsuda's approach to self-awareness is different from monika; instead she'd rather shackle and tame the narrative from within instead of breaking it through its rules.
# the scene ends rather abruptly with tsubaki giving an ominous implicaton on what she's going to do next. as to what...who knows?
# as for the player choice menus, thee should be exactly ONE explicit directive to tsubaki for her to do something, as that's what we've done up to this point.
# the other two options are natural dialogue that, if pressed, actually end up ABORTING the route at the last second. if tsubaki picks up on this, she acknowledges that you're no longer on the same wavelength and rewinds everything back to what the following day would be after the culture festival.
# tsubaki's speech patterns should be normal up to a certain point to where they become erratic, delirious, and even nonsensical at times.
# music used: audio.noreturn
# tsubaki sprites: post_neut and post_revelation (yes, a psychotic look that makes her look like she's had some sort of revelation)
# motifs: the planner, the coin flip, her hobby of washing coins